Dimensions, form, surfaces, and nanometre-scale comparisons (@met-dimensional-case: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metrology, #source "../sources/Dimensional-Metrology.lingua#r_5XRAV7WQWR6CTM94WM04G0Z647", #source "../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E", #source "../sources/SI-Realizations.lingua#r_240WHEHDVW9TR241AXP6T4STM0", #metrology "../practice/Reference-life-cycle.lingua#r_1ZS7B98GYPWX6S7BFZ5S6CY6YR", #mechanical-engineering "../../../engineering/mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/measurement/Inspection-decisions-sampling-and-nonconforming-parts.lingua#r_497ARAWRSTFZ7W09BGBJF80VMF") { r_66KYHH97TER9KH7NJJASWS9K5K
**Read:** [Fundamental Good Practice in Dimensional Metrology — Flack and Hannaford](../sources/Dimensional-Metrology.lingua#r_5XRAV7WQWR6CTM94WM04G0Z647), the entire guide; [Simple Guide for Evaluating and Expressing Uncertainty — Possolo](../sources/Uncertainty-NIST-1900.lingua#r_75WCVW8CJG4TAFD3330T87588E), E5 Gauge Blocks and E13 Thermal Expansion Coefficient; [Practical realizations of SI units — BIPM consultative committees](../sources/SI-Realizations.lingua#r_240WHEHDVW9TR241AXP6T4STM0), a full current metre or dimensional-nanometrology document.

Define the geometric feature and association rule before selecting a measurement technique. A two-point size, fitted cylinder, maximum material envelope, surface-height statistic, and pixel edge location are different quantities. Sampling locations, filtering, alignment, reference temperature, and deformation can affect the result as much as an instrument’s nominal resolution.

Read the complete dimensional guide, then study a practical realization or comparison relevant to a selected feature. For interferometric length, distinguish vacuum wavelength, refractive index, optical path, geometric alignment, and the actual surfaces defining the length. A laser specification alone does not determine the uncertainty of the finished dimensional result.

At small scales, a feature’s definition can depend strongly on the probe interaction or image-processing model. An optical edge, electron-image contrast boundary, and mechanical contact boundary need not represent the same physical surface without a relation and uncertainty. The BIPM dimensional-nanometrology guidance offers concrete cases involving silicon lattice information and monoatomic steps.

**Work:** reconstruct a gauge-block comparison from TN 1900 E5 and identify the corrections and shared effects. Then read one complete current dimensional realization or nanometrology guidance document. Draw its reference chain and derive a simplified uncertainty model with the physical assumptions explicit. Compare this with a macroscopic caliper study and explain why reading extra display digits does not reproduce the advanced capability.

For a technical drawing, connect tolerances, references, and an inspection strategy. State which aspects of form and surface are actually sampled and which are inferred. An advanced report should distinguish repeatability, uncertainty of the defined feature, and uncertainty introduced by an incomplete geometric sampling strategy.

**Continue:** [Produce, preserve, transfer, and replace the references](../practice/Reference-life-cycle.lingua#r_1ZS7B98GYPWX6S7BFZ5S6CY6YR).

